{286}{Well, a week or so later we were out to sea, and it was the new moon so it was dark, and a strange westerly had appeared, and brought in a bank of low clouds, thick as lamb stew...and then we saw the other ship, just a'restin' off the starboard.  Silent as death, and as still as if she was anchored...her sails tattered, her timbers rotted...and then we heard the screams...}{Well, a week or so later we were out to sea, and it was the new moon so it was dark, and a strange westerly had appeared, and brought in a bank of low clouds, thick as lamb stew...and then we saw the other ship, just a'restin' off the starboard.  Silent as death, and as still as if she was anchored...her sails tattered, her timbers rotted...and then we heard the screams...}{}{}{}{}
